<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Somalia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Somalia is a region in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horn-of-africa">Horn of Africa</a> along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-aden">Gulf of Aden</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a>. In antiquity it supplied aromatics such as frankincense and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/myrrh">myrrh</a>. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aksumite-empire">Aksumite Empire</a> list aromatics from Somalia among the goods traded through Aksum.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/somalia.jpg" alt="Somalia" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: see upload history · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Somalia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Many old stone-lined wells across southern <b>Somalia</b> are still attributed by local tradition to the Ajuran, centuries after the sultanate disappeared.</blockquote><a href="/empire/ajuran-sultanate">Ajuran Sultanate · At a glance</a></li><li><blockquote>…Liberation Front fought for Eritrean independence, rebels in Tigray included the nascent Tigray People's Liberation Front, and the Western Somali Liberation Front had by June 1977 driven the army out of much of the Ogaden into fortified towns before <b>Somalia</b> launched a full-scale invasion in the Ogaden War.</blockquote><a href="/empire/derg">Derg · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>The Treaty of Paris in 1947 formally stripped Italy of its colonies, although it returned to <b>Somalia</b> as a United Nations trustee from 1950 to 1960.</blockquote><a href="/empire/italian-empire">Italian Empire · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>Colonial expansion followed, with Eritrea organised as a colony in 1890 and a protectorate over much of <b>Somalia</b>, but the attempt to conquer Ethiopia ended in defeat at the Battle of Adwa in 1896.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-italy">Kingdom of Italy · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Malayan and Malaysian troops have served in United Nations missions from the Congo in the 1960s to <b>Somalia</b> and Bosnia in the 1990s and Lebanon.</blockquote><a href="/empire/malaysia">Malaysia · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1960 British Somaliland was independent for only five days, from 26 June to 1 July, before uniting with <b>Somalia</b>; Somaliland’s claim rests on that brief statehood.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-somaliland">Republic of Somaliland · At a glance</a></li></ul></section>
